From 88723f5136d2432e09995bebe5274437cb7be766 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Brett Morgan <brett.morgan@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 20:59:35 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] gcloud: document services list --limit gotcha and
 project/location setup

- Warn in Data Reduction Strategies that `gcloud services list` passes
  `--limit=N` to `serviceusage.ListServices` before client-side `--filter`
  runs, which truncates the alphabetical service list and hides enabled
  APIs later in the alphabet (`cloudbuild`, `firestore`, `run`) when
  combined with `--filter="config.name:(...)"`.
- Add `gcloud firestore locations list` to the Location Discovery examples.
- Expand `references/cli-usage.md` with project discovery (`gcloud projects list`),
  active project verification (`gcloud config get-value core/project`),
  ADC quota project synchronization (`gcloud auth application-default set-quota-project`),
  and Cloud Run default region configuration (`gcloud config set run/region`).
---
 skills/cloud/gcloud/SKILL.md                | 13 +++++++++++--
 skills/cloud/gcloud/references/cli-usage.md | 19 ++++++++++++++-----
 2 files changed, 25 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/skills/cloud/gcloud/SKILL.md b/skills/cloud/gcloud/SKILL.md
index c9b7cfb..54ad928 100644
--- a/skills/cloud/gcloud/SKILL.md
+++ b/skills/cloud/gcloud/SKILL.md
@@ -120,6 +120,14 @@ one data reduction flag (`--limit`, `--filter`, or `--format`).
     formats`.
 
 *   **Limiting**: Use `--limit=N` to cap the number of resources returned.
+    *Gotcha (`gcloud services list`)*: `gcloud services list` passes `--limit=N`
+    to `serviceusage.ListServices` **before** client-side `--filter` runs, so
+    combining `--limit=10` with `--filter="config.name:(...)"` only inspects the
+    first 10 enabled APIs alphabetically (e.g., `artifactregistry.googleapis.com`)
+    and drops matching services later in the alphabet (`cloudbuild`, `firestore`,
+    `run`). When filtering `gcloud services list` for specific APIs, use
+    `--filter="config.name:(...)"` and `--format="table(config.name,state)"`
+    without `--limit`.
 
 *   **Filtering**: Use `--filter` to narrow down results server-side. Prioritize
     `:` for pattern matching and never quote the right side of the colon. Treat
@@ -189,8 +197,9 @@ environment, they must explicitly provide project and location scoping.
         unified `locations list` command:
 
         *   `gcloud <GROUP> locations list --project=<PROJECT_ID>`
-        *   *Examples*: `gcloud artifacts locations list`, `gcloud kms locations
-            list`, `gcloud secrets locations list`.
+        *   *Examples*: `gcloud artifacts locations list`, `gcloud firestore
+            locations list --format="table(locationId,displayName)"`, `gcloud kms
+            locations list`, `gcloud secrets locations list`.
 
 ## Safety & Guardrails
 
diff --git a/skills/cloud/gcloud/references/cli-usage.md b/skills/cloud/gcloud/references/cli-usage.md
index 42525d1..6f29b0e 100644
--- a/skills/cloud/gcloud/references/cli-usage.md
+++ b/skills/cloud/gcloud/references/cli-usage.md
@@ -148,17 +148,26 @@ dev, staging, prod):
 
 Properties set default values for flags across `gcloud` invocations:
 
--   **Set active project:**
+-   **List available projects to find a project ID:**
 
     ```bash
-    gcloud config set core/project {project_id}
+    gcloud projects list --format="table(projectId,name,projectNumber)" --limit=20
     ```
 
--   **Set default compute region and zone:**
+-   **Set and verify active project (and ADC quota project):**
 
     ```bash
-    gcloud config set compute/region {region}
-    gcloud config set compute/zone {zone}
+    gcloud config set core/project {project_id} --quiet
+    gcloud config get-value core/project
+    gcloud auth application-default set-quota-project {project_id} --quiet
+    ```
+
+-   **Set default compute or Cloud Run region and zone:**
+
+    ```bash
+    gcloud config set compute/region {region} --quiet
+    gcloud config set compute/zone {zone} --quiet
+    gcloud config set run/region {region} --quiet
     ```
 
 -   **View all active configuration properties:**
